a 21 year old man who was stabbed to  death at the notting hill carnival has  been named today by his manager as  rapper takayo nambard the rapper from  bristol who went by the stage name  t-core stretch had been at the carnival  with his younger sister a warning that  the images we're about to show you were  taken in the moments after the rapper  was stabbed  while several officers tried to revive  him however he later died in hospital a  murder investigation is now underway and  police are appealing to festival goers  to come forward with any information  they may have a number of violent  incidents broke out at the end of this  year's carnival including several  serious stabbings marring the end of a  festival which was attended by more than  a million people  there were hundreds of people in the  immediate vicinity when this incident  took place  i would urge anyone who saw anything who  has video footage or who has any other  information that could assist officers  to come forward  tonight our thoughts are with the family  of the young man who has lost his life  in this senseless attack  uh joining us now from west london is  our crime correspondent martin brunt  who's following developments for us  martin talk to us about what's happening  in the police investigation at the  moment  as the hunt for the killer or killers  goes on no word from the metropolitan  police of an arrest and continuing  appeal for information uh the  metropolitan police have given more  details of um an escalation of violence  uh last night the second  day of the carnival and towards the  closing hours last night they told us  that there were apart from the fatal  stabbing six other stabbings in which  people were injured  this was on monday night  the second day  of the carnival and in previous  carnivals where there has been trouble  it's tended to come as darkness falls  towards the end of that that second day  they've also told us the met police that  there were 74 of their officers who were  injured  no real breakdown of the injuries but  some of those were the results say  the met police of assaults on those  officers and they've also  told us that there were 441  searches of people at the carnival now  as that  violence escalated on the second evening  police introduced special measures  section 60 which gave them the powers to  stop people at will without any specific  suspicion about those individuals so  over the two days there were 441  people who were stopped and searched  the other figures that the police gave  us earlier in the day remain the same  209 people were arrested  46 of them for assaults 36 for drugs  possession and 33 for the possession  of offensive weapons and uh there were  other  more minor um offences for which people  were arrested but so far  no word of any arrests in the major  thrust of this investigation for the  killer or killers
 

